--remove all csv file alone;

REMOVE @~/.*\.csv;
REMOVE @~ PATTERN = '.*\.csv';
REMOVE @~ PATTERN = '.*\.csv.gz';

-- remove pattern of file

REMOVE @~ PATTERN = 'customer_.*\.gz';


Diiferent ON_ERROR options in COPY_INTO option: 
===============================================
ABORT_STATEMENT - Default. If any error occurs, the entire load fails. No data is loaded.

CONTINUE - Skip problematic rows and continue loading remaining rows. Errors are recorded in load metadata.

SKIP_FILE - If any error occurs in a file, skip the entire file. Other files are processed.

SKIP_FILE_<n> - Skip the file only if the number of errors ≤ n. Otherwise, skip the file.

SKIP_FILE_NUM(n) - Same as above; newer form. Skip file if number of errors ≤ n

SKIP_FILE_NUM => n - Used in COPY INTO <location> syntax with arrow (=>) notation. 


Examples: 

   COPY INTO my_table FROM @my_stage FILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = 'CSV') ON_ERROR = 'CONTINUE';
   
   ON_ERROR = 'SKIP_FILE_2'; OR -- ON_ERROR = 'SKIP_FILE_NUM(2)';
   
   
